1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,969
Day 50: Jarvis, a voice assistant that needs no cloud AI.

2
00:00:05,419 --> 00:00:07,441
Jarvis runs only on local models.

3
00:00:07,441 --> 00:00:10,383
It keeps two memories: a diary of what happened,

4
00:00:10,383 --> 00:00:12,896
and a knowledge graph of what it learned.

5
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:15,434
A cheap local check first asks:

6
00:00:15,434 --> 00:00:18,735
does the current conversation already cover this?

7
00:00:18,735 --> 00:00:20,149
No model call needed.

8
00:00:20,599 --> 00:00:23,741
If not, the diary searches past conversations,

9
00:00:23,741 --> 00:00:27,633
while the graph holds durable facts under three branches:

10
00:00:27,633 --> 00:00:29,272
user, directives, world.

11
00:00:29,722 --> 00:00:31,616
Each branch grows as a tree.

12
00:00:31,616 --> 00:00:35,268
Past fifteen hundred tokens, a model splits a node and

13
00:00:35,268 --> 00:00:37,094
merges contradicting facts.

14
00:00:37,544 --> 00:00:41,691
Results land straight in the system prompt for the next reply,

15
00:00:41,691 --> 00:00:43,431
no extra tool call needed.

16
00:00:43,881 --> 00:00:45,821
On a local GPU with Ollama,

17
00:00:45,821 --> 00:00:48,911
all fifty-one knowledge graph evals passed.

18
00:00:48,911 --> 00:00:51,929
When we said we moved from Tokyo to Osaka,

19
00:00:51,929 --> 00:00:54,157
the graph rewrote the old fact,

20
00:00:54,157 --> 00:00:56,385
yet reported zero facts stored.

21
00:00:56,835 --> 00:00:59,295
The Zenn article has the full logs and

22
00:00:59,295 --> 00:01:00,914
the no-mock demo scripts.

23
00:01:00,914 --> 00:01:03,893
Free for non-commercial use; source on GitHub.
